    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-Assistant-postdoctoral/1434670533/": {
      "title": "University Assistant postdoctoral",
      "description": "University Assistant postdoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University Assistant postdoctoral The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. Fueled by curiosity and a deep sense of duty, they contribute invaluable insights to research and teaching, enriching our society. Are you inspired and driven by the desire to make a meaningful impact? We are currently seeking a/an University Assistant postdoctoral 47 Faculty of Psychology Job vacancy starting:  | Working hours:  40.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6150 At the University of Vienna, more than 10,000 people work together towards answering the big questions of the future. Around 7,700 of them are scientists who, with their curiosity and continuous demand for excellence, conduct top-level international research and teaching. Are you also looking for the right space to develop your potential? We are seeking a/an Your place of work: The Faculty of Psychology at the University of Vienna comprises the Dean's Office, a Student Service Center, four institutes, and the Outpatient Unit for Research, Teaching and Practice. Your future position is based with the new Professorship of Psychotherapy and Psychotherapy Research (Univ.-Prof. Dr. Thomas Probst) at the Institute for Clinical and Health Psychology. The research group investigates Processes and Effectiveness of Psychotherapy and Therapeutic Interventions. Other key research areas of the professorship include: Evidence-Based Psychotherapy Digitalization, e.g., AI, in Psychotherapy The Use of Psychological and Neuroscientific Methods in Psychotherapy Research The working group actively promotes open and reproducible science (e.g., through pre-registration and the sharing of materials and data) and values diverse perspectives. Your future tasks: Active participation in research, teaching & administration, which means: You strengthen the research profile in the field of psychotherapy research. You support research activities on the use of artificial intelligence in psychotherapy. You plan and conduct your own scientific studies. You publish articles in international peer-reviewed journals. You give presentations at national and international scientific conferences. You participate in science communication activities. You apply for projects and raise third-party funds. You hold courses independently within the scope of the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement . You supervise students. You participate in evaluation measures and in quality assurance. You take on administrative tasks in research and teaching. This is part of your personality: Completed doctoral/PhD studies in psychology or other related fields. Experience in research projects on human-AI interaction, preferably in a therapeutic context. In-depth knowledge of  AI, LLM, Conversational AI (voicebots, chatbots, AI avatars, AI videos, AI voices). In-depth knowledge of advanced statistical methods (e.g., multilevel modeling). Proven research competence and initiative through international publications in peer-reviewed journals. Knowledge of relevant AI software. Ability to work in an interdisciplinary team. Leadership skills and ability to work in a team. Diligent, independent work methods. Strong sense of responsibility. Excellent written and spoken English and German skills (C1). Desirable qualifications are: Experience with and interest in innovative study-designs for investigating the potential benefits of artificial intelligence in psychotherapy. Knowledge of programming languages is a plus. Psychotherapy training (whether currently in progress or completed) is a plus. Work experience with clinical or mentally distressed populations is a plus. Knowledge of psychophysiology is a plus. What we offer: Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible working hours, remote/hybrid upon agreement. Inspiring working atmosphere: You are part of a friendly and supportive team with excellent research infrastructure and connections to other interdisciplinary research initiatives. We will help you refine your research profile and actively support your professional development. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fixed-term contract and fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 5.014,30 (14 times a year) increases if we can credit professional experience. We offer an initial contract for three years. This contract can be extended to six years in total by mutual agreement. Good public transport connections: Your workplace is easily accessible by public transport. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: We look forward to receiving your detailed application with a letter of motivation as well as an outline of a planned research project (max. two pages). Please include your academic CV in tabular form (including your list of publications and a list of courses and lectures you have given). PDF attachments of publications, awards/prizes (if applicable). Contact details of of at least two people who could provide reference letters. Degree certificates, official notifications. Via our job portal/ Apply now - button. If you have any questions, please contact: Thomas Probst thomas. probst @univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity. We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 10/15/2026 Post Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: postdoctoral, Postdoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our