    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-Assistant-postdoctoral/1444400533/": {
      "title": "University Assistant postdoctoral",
      "description": "University Assistant postdoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. Fueled by curiosity and a deep sense of duty, they contribute invaluable insights to research and teaching, enriching our society. Are you inspired and driven by the desire to make a meaningful impact? We are currently seeking a/an University Assistant postdoctoral 45 Faculty of Philological and Cultural Studies Job vacancy starting: 12/01/2026 | Working hours:  40.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: 11/30/2032 Job ID: 6032 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where over 7,500 brilliant minds have found a unique balance of freedom and support. Join us if you’re passionate about groundbreaking international research and academic excellence. Ready to be part of our team? Let’s shape the future together! Your personal sphere of play: As a Postdoctoral University Assistant, you will join the research team led by Univ.-Prof. Dr. Hartmut Wulfram. The Department of Classical Philology, Medieval and Neo-Latin Studies is dedicated to research and teaching across the languages and literatures of Greek and Roman Antiquity (including Late Antiquity), as well as Late, Medieval, and Neo-Latin language and post-antique Latin literature up to the present day—a span of approximately 2,700 years. At the core of its mission is language training in Greek and Latin, alongside the literary analysis and textual interpretation of works from European Antiquity that have significantly shaped, and continue to influence, world culture. Student education is delivered within the framework of bachelor's and master's degree programs, teacher education programs (Latin and/or Greek), and doctoral degree programs in Greek and/or Latin. Your future tasks: You will actively contribute to research, teaching, and administration: You will develop an independent research profile in the field of Neo-Latin Philology (preferably Italian Humanism). You will prepare and complete a publishable habilitation thesis (following a dissertation in Neo-Latin, this may also be in Classical Latin Studies). You will publish internationally and deliver conference presentations and lectures. You will independently teach courses to the extent stipulated by the collective bargaining agreement. You will undertake administrative responsibilities in research (e.g., assisting in the organization of conferences) and teaching (e.g., serving on academic committees). Your Profile & Qualifications: Completed doctoral/PhD degree in Latin Studies, alongside a documented interest in Neo-Latin Philology and the Latin reception tradition. Outstanding doctoral dissertation in the field of Classical Latin Studies or Neo-Latin Philology. Didactic competence and teaching skills. Proficient IT user skills (especially MS Office). Team player with strong social and communication skills. Language Proficiencies: Latin: Excellent command Ancient Greek: Basic knowledge German: Excellent command English: Very good command Italian: Very good reading comprehension French: Very good reading comprehension What we offer: Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible working hours, remote/hybrid and/or part-time work (upon agreement). Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Good public transport connections: Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fixed-term contract and fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 5.014,30 (14 times a year) for a period of 6 years / 72 months increases if we can credit professional experience. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: Academic curriculum vitae (CV) List of publications Outline of the habilitation project (max. 1 page) Official degree certificate / confirmation of completed doctoral/PhD studies Via our job portal / \"Apply Now\" button If you have any questions, please contact: Hartmut Wulfram hartmut.wulfram@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 10/26/2026 Post Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: postdoctoral Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
