    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Excavation-technician/1433551533/": {
      "title": "Excavation technician",
      "description": "Excavation technician Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Excavation technician At the University of Vienna, almost 11,000 individuals explore the mysteries that shape our future. Among them, approximately 3,000 dedicated employees provide administrative and technical support for cutting-edge international research and teaching. With us you will discover a nurturing environment that encourages your continuous aspiration to discover and shape innovative solutions. Does this resonate with your ambitions? We are currently seeking a/an Excavation technician 40 Faculty of Historical and Cultural Studies Job vacancy starting: 01/01/2027 | Working hours: 40.00  | Classification CBA: §54 VwGr. IIIb Limited contract until: Job ID: 6139 If you love to conduct archaeological excavations, then welcome to the team! Our department consists of personalities who want to make a change. Our work is based on respectful communication, professionalism and high aspirations of having a positive impact on society. Your personal sphere of influence: The Department of Prehistory and Historical Archaeology is advertising a post in excavation techniques and archaeological building research (Chair of Historical Archaeology, Prof. Dr Thomas Kühtreiber). The post is closely linked to the ongoing research programmes ‘Dynamics in Rural Areas’ and ‘Identities and Material Cultures’ at the Chair of Historical Archaeology. Your future tasks: The excavation technician is expected to assist the Chair of Historical Archaeology with the administration and execution of archaeological fieldwork. This involves the organisation, conduct, documentation and reporting of teaching and research excavations, as well as practical sessions and work placements in archaeological building research and comparable activities. Technical supervision of the excavation, independent documentation (including using a total station and image-based modelling, e.g. with drones), management of artefact records, creation of Harris matrices, and contribution to Parts A and B of the excavation report in accordance with BDA guidelines Independently producing plans (including photographic plans) for archaeological building documentation Participation in teaching excavations and building research courses This is part of your personality: Successful candidates must hold a Bachelor’s degree in Prehistory and Historical Archaeology or a related archaeological discipline before taking up the position (the Bachelor’s degree must have been obtained by the date of appointment at the latest). You will have knowledge of medieval and modern archaeology, demonstrated through relevant training or practical experience (e.g. a Bachelor’s thesis on a relevant topic, participation in relevant excavations, building surveys or research projects). You will have practical experience in conducting stratigraphic excavations, including the creation of Harris matrices (to be demonstrated by a list of projects). You have in-depth knowledge of surveying techniques, digital documentation and analysis in excavations and/or building research projects (evidence to be provided in the form of a list of projects). You have knowledge of administration and reporting in archaeological excavations and/or building research (evidence to be provided in the form of a list of projects). You have demonstrable knowledge of image-based modelling, CAD systems and geographic information systems (preferably QGIS). You have experience of working in a team and on interdisciplinary research projects. Proficiency in German (minimum C1) is required; written and spoken English (minimum B2) forms an important basis for your work. A Category B driving licence is essential. What we offer: Contract duration : The job vacany starts with January 1st, 2027. The contract is limited until: 31.12.2027 with option to convert to a permanent contract Fair salary : The monthly gross salary is 3.131,30 € (14x/year, Allg. Personal IIIb, Grundstufe). Prior experience can be taken into account. Work-life balance : The position is full-time, with a standard working week of 40 hours. We offer flexible working hours and place great importance on arranging working time by mutual agreement, taking into account both operational requirements and the personal needs of our employees, particularly with regard to caregiving responsibilities. Inspiring working atmosphere : You are part of a committed team with diverse university backgrounds in a relaxed work environment. Good public transport connections : Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. The place of work is Vienna, unless you are traveling for research purposes. A workspace in a shared office will be provided. Internal further training : Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Equal opportunities for all : We welcome every additional personality to the team! It’s that easy to apply: Applications can be submitted in German and must include letter of motivation (max. 2 pages) CV a list of previous excavation and building research activities, with a particular focus on administrative tasks (e.g. on-site excavation management, artefact management, reporting) and digital documentation work Evidence (certificates, diplomas) of training in digital documentation techniques (CAD, GIS, Image Based Modelling) Leaving certificates Further documents, if necessary. If you have any content questions, please contact: Thomas Kühtreiber thomas.kuehtreiber@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of  Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection Application deadline: 10/31/2026 Laboratory & Technology Apply now » Find similar jobs: Laboratory & Technology, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
