    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Postdoc-for-Astronomical-Observing-Programs-at-the-Leopold-Figl-Observatory/1433430933/": {
      "title": "Postdoc for Astronomical Observing Programs",
      "description": "Postdoc for Astronomical Observing Programs at the Leopold Figl Observatory Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc for Astronomical Observing Programs at the Leopold Figl Observatory At the University of Vienna, almost 11,000 people work together on the big questions of the future. Approximately 7,700 of them are academic staff members. These are individuals who, with their curiosity and their continuous pursuit of excellence, engage in international cutting-edge research and teaching. With us, you will also find space to unfold your potential. We are looking for a ... Postdoc for Astronomical Observing Programs at the Leopold Figl Observatory 53 Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography and Astronomy Job vacancy starting: 01/01/2027 | Working hours:  40.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6123 The Leopold Figl Observatory for Astrophysics , operated by the Department of Astrophysics of the University of Vienna, hosts the largest optical telescope in Austria (1.5 m). Within the Figl 2030 project , the observatory is building up a major observing program for the follow-up and characterization of transiting extrasolar planets. We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher to join the team behind this program. You will work in close collaboration with colleagues at the Department of Astrophysics, in particular Univ.-Prof. Dr. João Alves and Dr. Stefan Meingast . Your working place: The Department of Astrophysics with currently around 100 members is part of the Faculty of Earth Sciences, Geography and Astronomy at the University of Vienna. You will be at the center of the Figl 2030 project, which dedicates a large share of the observing time of the 1.5 m Leopold Figl telescope to the photometric follow-up of transiting exoplanet candidates identified by space missions such as TESS and PLATO. This includes false-positive screening and the refinement of transit parameters. The telescope is currently being upgraded with a new wide-field camera system. You will be based at the University Observatory in Vienna and help build up the observing program, including taking observations yourself. The team observes mostly remotely from Vienna, with occasional work at the telescope on Mitterschöpfl. The position is set for 48 months , with a preferred starting date of January 1, 2027 . Your future tasks: Active participation in research, teaching & administration, which means: As part of a team, you help establish and operate observing programs — in particular those related to exoplanet research — at the 1.5 m Leopold Figl telescope. You build up your research profile in time-domain science with room for independent projects and collaborations. You participate in the commissioning and science verification of the new wide-field camera system. You develop, maintain, and document the data reduction and photometry pipelines required for high-precision time-series photometry. You help coordinate the observatory’s participation in international follow-up programs (e.g., for NASA’s TESS mission). You lead and participate in scientific publications in peer-reviewed journals and present results at international meetings. You contribute to the outreach activities. You can (co-)supervise Bachelor and Master students and involve students in the observations. You can hold courses independently within the scope of the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement. Your profile: Must-haves A PhD degree in astronomy, astrophysics, or a closely related field, completed by the starting date. Experience with optical astronomical observations. Experience with high-precision photometry and/or time-series analysis. Research experience in observational astronomy, demonstrated through publications appropriate to your career stage. Solid programming skills (e.g., Python) and experience with astronomical data processing. Fluency in English (spoken and written). A category B driver’s license (Austrian Führerschein B or an equivalent from another country), or the willingness to obtain one before or shortly after the start of the position. Good-to-haves Experience with exoplanet transit observations and light curve modeling. Experience with telescope operations, instrument commissioning, or remote observing. Experience with infrared astronomical observations. Hands-on technical or engineering experience, for example with observatory hardware, instrumentation, electronics, or mechanical systems, whether from astronomy or another field. Experience in the supervision of students and in public outreach. Knowledge of German. Your working style is independent, structured, and solution-oriented. You thrive in collaborative, international teams and enjoy tackling technical challenges in dynamic environments. You are a team player and have good social and communicative skills. What we offer: Inspiring working atmosphere: You have the opportunity to work within a dedicated team on forefront science, while profiting from the international environment in the Department of Astrophysics. We have privileged access to the Austrian Scientific Computing (ASC) super-computing facility. As a member state of ESO and ESA , Austria has access to their first-class observing facilities, and the Department of Astrophysics is a partner in three instrument consortia for ESO’s Extremely Large Telescope (ELT), currently under construction. Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible working hours. Upon agreement, hybrid working hours within Austria might be possible up to a certain extent. Good public transport connections: Your working place, the University Observatory, is located in the middle of the natural monument Observatory Park in the lively city of Vienna with outstanding public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fixed-term contract and fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 5.014,30 (14 times a year) increases if we can credit professional experience. Equal opportunities for all: We look forward to diverse personalities in the team! It is that easy to apply: With your CV including a list of publications A letter of motivation A brief description of your research interests Contact details of references who may be contacted regarding your application With your PhD certificate Via our job portal/ Apply now -  button If you have any questions, please contact: Stefan Meingast stefan.meingast@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 10/15/2026 [[filter3]] [[custAlternativeApplyURL]] Apply now » Find similar jobs: postdoctoral, Postdoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Go