    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Full-Professor-of-Arabic-Studies/1443072833/": {
      "title": "The position:",
      "description": "Full Professor of Arabic Studies Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » The University of Vienna is internationally renowned for its excellence in teaching and research, and counts more than 7,500 academics from all disciplines. This breadth of expertise offers unique opportunities to address the complex challenges of modern society, to develop comprehensive new approaches, and educate the problem-solvers of tomorrow from a multidisciplinary perspective. At the Faculty of Philological and Cultural Studies, the University of Vienna invites applications for a Full Professor of Arabic Studies The position: The successful candidate should represent the field of Arabic Studies, with a focus on linguistics, in its full range in both research and teaching, and have a proven track record of international excellence. We expect a philologically and linguistically grounded research profile covering written Arabic such as Classical Arabic, Modern Standard Arabic, Middle Arabic, and/or spoken varieties of Arabic, in the fields of edition philology, contact linguistics, corpus linguistics, sociolinguistics, text linguistics etc. In teaching, the successful candidate will offer courses in Classical Arabic and Modern Arabic, as well as topics related to the Arab world, dialectology, and general linguistic approaches. S/he will also contribute to, and share responsibility for, teaching in the BA programme “Oriental Studies”, the MA programme “Arab World Studies: Language and Society”, and, particularly, the MA programme “Arabic Linguistics”. Knowledge of one Arabic dialect, preferably from the East of the Arab world, is therefore required. The successful candidate is also expected to contribute to the Faculty’s doctoral programme and to existing research initiatives, such as the Vienna Corpus of Arabic Varieties (VICAV), developed in collaboration with the Austrian Academy of Sciences. Your academic profile: •    Doctoral degree/PhD •    Outstanding research achievements, excellent publication and funding record, international reputation •    Experience in designing and managing large research projects •    Excellent teaching and supervision skills at the bachelor's, master's, and doctoral level •    Proven leadership qualities •    Gender and diversity competence •    Willingness to take on organisational and administrative responsibilities within the Faculty/Centre and/or the University The University of Vienna expects the successful candidate to acquire, within three years, proficiency in German sufficient for teaching in bachelor’s programmes and for participation in university committees. We offer: a dynamic research environment a wide range of research and teaching support services attractive working conditions in a city with a high quality of life an attractive salary according to the Collective Bargaining Agreement for University Staff (§98 UG, level A1, to be negotiated individually) and an organisational retirement plan a “start-up package”, in particular for the initiation of research projects comprehensive and personalised support for newly appointed professors and their families throughout their move and transition to Vienna Get off to a great start in your new job: the Welcome Compass helps you settle into your new role at the University of Vienna and life in Vienna. Application documents: Please submit a single PDF file (LastName_FirstName.pdf) containing the following information in English via e-mail to the Dean of the Faculty of Philological and Cultural Studies, Stephan Müller ( dekanat.philkult@univie.ac.at ): 1. Letter of motivation 2. Academic curriculum vitae o    education and training o    positions held to date o    career breaks (e.g. parental, family or other care periods) o    awards and honours o    commissions of trust o    previous and current cooperation partners o    list of most important acquired third-party funding as principal investigator, and, if applicable, of inventions/patents o    list of most important scientific talks (max. 10) o    list of courses taught (presented in a clear, concise format) o    supervision activities (Master and PhD) 3. List of publications and a link to your ORCID record 4. Research statement o    most important research achievements (max. 2 pages) and planned future research activities (max. 4 pages) o    synopsis of five key publications with relevance to the position advertised 5. Teaching and supervision statement o    teaching and supervision concept, with particular reference to teaching and learning methods, diverse student audiences, class sizes and types of courses (max. 2 pages) Appendices to application document: a. Five key publications as electronic full text version b. Teaching evaluations (if available, compiled into a single PDF file) c. Copies of certificates of academic degrees (mandatory, compiled into a single PDF file) The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Privacy Policy Reference no.: 6278 Application deadline: 12/15/2026 Professorship Vacancies dekanat.philkult@univie.ac.at Apply now » Find similar jobs: Full Professorships, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your 