    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Vienna-Doctoral-School-of-Microbiology-and-Environmental-Science-Doctoral-Positions-%28AUTUMN-CALL-2/1431157933/": {
      "title": "Jobs in Research & Teaching",
      "description": "Vienna Doctoral School of Microbiology and Environmental Science - Doctoral Positions (AUTUMN CALL 2 Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. Fuelled by curiosity and a deep sense of responsibility, they provide invaluable contributions to research and teaching, thus enriching our society. Are you also inspired and driven by the desire to make a meaningful impact? Vienna Doctoral School of Microbiology and Environmental Science - Doctoral Positions (AUTUMN CALL 2026) Centre for Microbiology and Environmental Systems Science Job vacancy starting:  | Working hours: 30 | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6169 The University of Vienna invites outstanding candidates to apply for mulitple doctoral positions in the Vienna Doctoral School of Microbiology and Environmental Science as part of its Autumn Call 2026 , offering multiple funded doctoral positions in total. Your personal sphere of influence: You will join ActiveSOIL, an international project funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation, dedicated to harnessing biology for climate-resilient and healthy soils. Based at the Centre for Microbiology and Environmental Systems Science (CeMESS) at the University of Vienna, you’ll work alongside partners in Aalborg (DK), Oxford (UK) and Berkeley (USA) to answer a fundamental question: how fast do microorganisms cycle nutrients in soil and which microbes drive it? Your future tasks: You will measure gross soil process rates, from depolymerisation to mineralisation, and link them to microbial identity, community composition and ultimately soil health, by combining stable isotope pool dilution assays with measurements of microbial community activity, generating the process-rate data that sits at the heart of the project. The work spans both demanding lab and field campaigns, giving you hands-on ownership of the full pipeline from sample collection to data interpretation. This is part of your personality: You bring a background in soil science, microbial ecology, or biogeochemistry, and a MSc degree in a related field, paired with genuine enthusiasm for rigorous, hands-on lab and field work.” Prior experience with isotope pool dilution assays, mass spectrometry, or microbial growth measurements is a plus but not a must-have, as you will be trained in these methods. What matters most is curiosity, resilience under demanding fieldwork conditions, a collaborative mindset for working across an international team, and a commitment to communicating your research through publications. What we offer: The successful candidate will be embedded in the Soil Ecology Group of Andreas Richter ( https://ter.univie.ac.at/richter ) at CeMESS, an internationally renowned centre in microbial ecology, soil ecology, and ecosystem science. The Centre offers a diverse and stimulating work environment. The PhD candidate will be enrolled in the Doctoral School in Microbiology and Environmental Science, which offers interdisciplinary training at the interfaces of microbiology, ecology and environmental science. The candidate will work at the forefront of soil health research, at the intersection of soil ecology and microbial biogeochemistry. Excellence in research : Join one of Europe’s leading universities with internationally recognised scholars. Vibrant research environment : Engage with top research groups, archives, libraries, and crossdisciplinary centres—supported by seminar series, colloquia, and visiting fellows. Structured doctoral training : Benefit from close supervision and gain access to high-quality methods workshops, transferable skills development, and opportunities to present your work and receive expert feedback. Fair salary : A basic gross salary of EUR 3.714,80 (on a 40h/week basis) per month, 14 times a year. Model 2 : The employment duration is 4 years. Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first\n12 months by submitting a non-extension declaration. International networks : Connect to a global community and collaborative projects that encourage mobility and knowledge exchange. Inclusive culture : We foster equal opportunity, diversity, and a collegial environment where talent thrives. It is that easy to apply (in English): To apply for this position, you must submit a complete application through the job portal of the University of Vienna (apply now-button). Complete applications include the following: Personal information and contact details Information on education, training, and professional experience Motivation statement Curriculum vitae Cover letter Master Degree / Diploma Application deadline: 15 October 2026, 14 am CET If you have any questions, please refer to the FAQs on the call website . Job seekers in need of a reasonable accommodation to complete the application process should call +43-1-4277-18248 or email phdcareers@univie.ac.at with their request. If you have any questions, please contact: Nadja Holzleitner vds-mes.cemess@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team!\nThe University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity. We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Application deadline: 10/15/2026 Prae Doc https://careers.univie.ac.at/en/praedoc/autumn-call Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy