      "title": "Jobs in Research & Teaching",
      "description": "Vienna Doctoral School of Pharmaceutical, Nutritional and Sport Sciences – Three Doctoral Positions Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » The University of Vienna is a community of almost 11,000 individuals, including approximately 7,700 academic staff members, who passionately pursue answers to the profound questions that shape our future. Fuelled by curiosity and a deep sense of responsibility, they provide invaluable contributions to research and teaching, thus enriching our society. Are you also inspired and driven by the desire to make a meaningful impact? Vienna Doctoral School of Pharmaceutical, Nutritional and Sport Sciences – Three Doctoral Positions (AUTUMN CALL 2026) Faculty of Life Sciences Job vacancy starting:  | Working hours: 30 | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6168 The University of Vienna invites outstanding candidates to apply for three doctoral positions in the Vienna Doctoral School of Pharmaceutical, Nutritional and Sport Sciences as part of its Autumn Call 2026 , offering eleven funded doctoral positions in total. Your personal sphere of influence: We are looking for outstanding international early-career researchers interested in pursuing doctoral research in the Vienna Doctoral School of Pharmaceutical, Nutritional and Sport Sciences (VDS-PhaNuSpo) of the University of Vienna as part of its Autumn Call 2026 . Interested candidates can apply for a PhD position under the supervision of one of the following three supervisors in: Empirical Educational Research in Sport Please note that the project should be embedded in the German-speaking educational context. Supervisor: Maike Niehues PhD programme in Sport Science Preferred Start date: 01/11/2026 Physical Literacy, Physical Activity and Health Education Supervisor: Johannes Carl PhD programme in Sport Science Preferred Start date: 01/11/2026 For 1 & 2: The employment duration is 4 years. Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a non-extension declaration. Molecular Drug Targeting Supervisor: Christoph Rademacher Doctoral programme in Pharmaceutical Sciences Preferred start date: 01/11/2026 The employment duration is 3 years. Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 3 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a declaration of non-extension. With appropriate work progress, an extension to a total maximum of 4 years is possible. Successful candidates will join the VDS-PhaNuSpo that brings together doctoral candidates and researchers from diverse disciplines and offers a structured doctoral programme, first-class supervision, vibrant research networks, opportunities to publish, teach, and engage internationally. Your future tasks: Participation in research projects/research studies Development and implementation of an independent doctoral research project Dissemination of project results in peer-reviewed publications and presentations at national conferences Participation in teaching and independent teaching of courses as defined by the collective agreement Supervision of students Contribution to the organisation of meetings, conferences, and symposia Involvement in department administration Strong communication, data presentation, and visualisation skills Ability to work both independently and collaboratively This is part of your personality: You are invited to apply if you are a highly qualified graduate who: has completed a Diploma or Bachelor’s and Master’s degree in a field of announced position of interest, or a closely related discipline; demonstrates a strong interest in academic research and in pursuing a PhD at the University of Vienna; meets the doctoral admission requirements of the University of Vienna by the start of employment. What we offer: Excellence in research: Join one of Europe’s leading universities with internationally recognised scholars. Vibrant research environment: Engage with top research groups, archives, libraries, and cross disciplinary centres—supported by seminar series, colloquia, and visiting fellows. Structured doctoral training: Benefit from close supervision and gain access to high-quality methods workshops, transferable skills development, and opportunities to present your work and receive expert feedback. Fair salary: A basic gross salary of monthly EUR 3.776,10 (on a 40h/week basis, 14x p.a.). Employment duration: See section ‘Your personal sphere of influence’. International networks: Connect to a global community and collaborative projects that encourage mobility and knowledge exchange. Inclusive culture: We foster equal opportunity, diversity, and a collegial environment where talent thrives. It is that easy to apply (in English): To apply for this position, you must submit a complete application through the job portal of the University of Vienna (apply now-button). Complete applications include the following: Personal information and contact details Letter of motivation Scientific Curriculum Vitae Information and Certificates of university degrees and ECT transcripts Information on additional training, professional experience Contact details of references Application deadline: 15 October 2026, 14 am CET If you have any questions, please refer to the FAQs on the call website . Job seekers in need of a reasonable accommodation to complete the application process should call +43-1-4277-18248 or email phdcareers@univie.ac.at with their request. If you have any questions, please contact: Isolde Prommer vds.phanuspo@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team!\nThe University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity. We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Application deadline: 10/15/2026 Prae Doc https://careers.univie.ac.at/en/praedoc/autumn-call Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off F