    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/Vienna-Doctoral-School-in-Cognition%2C-Behavior%2C-and-Neuroscience-Doctoral-Positions-%28AUTUMN-CALL-20/1431139533/": {
      "title": "Jobs in Research & Teaching",
      "description": "Vienna Doctoral School in Cognition, Behavior, and Neuroscience - Doctoral Positions (AUTUMN CALL 20 Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » At the University of Vienna, over 10,000 people work together on the big questions of the future. Approximately 7,500 of them are academic staff members. These are individuals who, with their curiosity and their continuous pursuit of excellence, engage in international cutting-edge research and teaching. With us, you will also find space to unfold your potential. We are looking for a/an Vienna Doctoral School in Cognition, Behavior, and Neuroscience - Doctoral Positions (AUTUMN CALL 2026) Faculty of Life Sciences Job vacancy starting: 01. März 2027 | Working hours: 30 | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6167 With this topically open call the Vienna Doctoral School in Cognition, Behavior and Neuroscience (VDS CoBeNe) at the University of Vienna is looking for highly motivated PhD candidates with innovative ideas. The VDS CoBeNe doctoral fellows will perform cutting-edge research with options to bridge fields and use an interdisciplinary approach. We offer 2 University Assistant (pre doc) positions for 3 years under the team supervision of two CoBeNe principle investigators of any of our research fields. Any PI of the CoBeNe faculty listed on the Autumn Call website could become your supervisor! The second supervisor can be added to the PhD project after the selection process. The uniting theme is the interest in human and non-human behavior, understanding its underlying cognitive, emotional, social, cultural, physiological, and neurobiological bases, studying how the brain maintains or changes functionality over time, and probing its evolutionary origins and development. Our PhD program is tailored to individual career tracks and includes continuous mentoring schemes, multiple opportunities for national and international scientific networking, and transferable skills training for enhancing careers inside and outside academia. Your personal sphere of influence: As an university assistant pre doc, you will take over tasks like: Planning and execution of empirical studies. Publication of research results in international scientific journals. Presentation of research results at national and international conferences. Participation in the acquisition of new research projects. Participation in administration. Your future tasks: You actively participate in research, teaching & administration, which means: You are involved in research projects and scientific studies. We expect you to finalize your dissertation agreement within 6-12 months. You work on your dissertation and its completion. You engage in teaching (independent and/or in a team) as defined by the collective agreement. You can be involved in the organization of meetings, conferences, or workshops. This is part of your personality: Must-haves: Master’s degree or equivalent in one of the respective study fields, the degree certificate must be available before being accepted into the doctoral program (latest June 2027) Not enrolled in the doctoral study program Have not previously applied for the CoBeNe uni:docs call Project must be supervised by 2 CoBeNe PIs (2nd supervisor to be selected at later stage) High level of both spoken and written English (official certificate not required) Nice to have: Very good ability to present and process research questions in a structured way Ability to work independently and as part of a team Publications or basic experience in scientific work and research methods Basic skills in scientific programming Knowledge of academic processes and structures Experience abroad (research, study, or both) Teaching experience What we offer: We aim to fill the position by 01 March 2027 latest by 01 June 2027. The employment duration is 3 years. Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 3 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a non-extension declaration. Job grading in accordance with collective bargaining agreement: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) with relevant work experience determining the assignment to a particular salary grade ( Salary scheme ). Work-life balance: Our employees enjoy flexible, family-friendly working hours, remote/hybrid (upon agreement). Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Good public transport connections: Your workplace in the center of beautiful Vienna is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3.714,80 (on a full-time basis; 14 times a year) increases if we can credit professional experience. Equal opportunities for everyone: We look forward to diverse personalities in the team! It is that easy to apply (in English): To apply for this position, you must submit a complete application through the job portal of the University of Vienna (apply now-button). Complete applications include the following documents in English: A 5-pages PhD proposal, max. 15.000 characters (including spaces). Motivation letter explaining why you apply to VDS CoBeNe and addressing your motivation and qualifications. Clearly indicate your desired research area. (max. 2 page). Select 1-2 VDS CoBeNe principal investigators (potential supervisors) that you wish to work with and details of two referees, at least one who has previously supervised you. Copies of bachelor’s and master’s degree certificates in German or in certified English translation in addition to their original language. Self-translated transcripts of your certificates will not be recognized (including credit transcripts) Please add additional documents if they proof relevant skills (awards, internships/participation in research projects, programming languages, lab techniques, transferable skills etc.) Application deadline: 15 October 2026, 14 am CET If you have any questions, please refer to the FAQs on the call website . Job seekers in need of a reasonable accommodation to complete the application process should call +43-1-4277-18248 or email phdcareers@univie.ac.at with their request. If you have any questions, please contact: Katja Hellekes vds.cobene@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team!\nThe University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities, the advancement of women and diversity. We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Application deadline: 10/15/2026 Prae Doc https://careers.univie.ac.at/en/praedoc/autumn-call Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled Vimeo Vimeo is a video hosting, sharing, and services platform focused on the delivery of video. Opting out of Vimeo cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with Vimeo videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider Vimeo Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled AddThis Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider AddThis Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
