    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral/1439308033/": {
      "title": "University assistant predoctoral",
      "description": "University assistant predoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University assistant predoctoral At the University of Vienna almost 11,000 personalities work together towards answering the big questions of the future. Around 7,700  of them do research and teaching, around 3,000 work in administration and organisation. We are looking for a/an University assistant predoctoral 30 Faculty of Catholic Theology Job vacancy starting: 02/10/2027 | Working hours: 30.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: 02/09/2031 Job ID: 6220 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where more than 7,700 academics thrive on curiosity in continuous exploration and help us better understand our world. Does this sound like you? Then join our accomplished team! Your personal sphere of influence: As a Praedoc University Assistant, you will join the team in the Department of Liturgical Studies and Sacramental Theology at the Department of Historical Theology within the Faculty of Catholic Theology at the University of Vienna (Department Chair: Univ.-Prof. Dr. Hans-Jürgen Feulner) and take on responsibilities such as actively participating in teaching as well as conducting your own research and publishing work. In addition, the department contributes to the internationally renowned open-access journal ( Ex Fonte ). We place great value on a collegial and harmonious work environment and encourage both social and academic exchange. You can find an overview of our team and our areas of academic research here: https://lit-ktf.univie.ac.at Your future tasks: You will actively participate in research, teaching, and administration, which means: Preparing a dissertation in our Department of Liturgical Studies and Sacramental Theology (signing a dissertation agreement within 12–18 months) Your own scholarly activities (primarily writing a dissertation) will be supported and encouraged. Participation in the department’s research projects and scholarly publications Presentations at conferences Participation in and independent teaching of courses in accordance with the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement Co-supervision of students Assistance in organizing conferences and study trips Participation in teaching and research administration Support for the open-access journal Ex Fonte This is part of your personality: Requirements: Completed master’s degree or diploma in Catholic Theology Excellent written and spoken German Good written and spoken English Good knowledge of Latin Ability to work independently and take responsibility for results Comprehensive computer skills, particularly in MS Office You are a team player with strong social and communication skills. Desirable qualifications: Completed diploma or master’s thesis in the field of Liturgical Studies Knowledge of an additional modern foreign language Knowledge of the Roman liturgy Knowledge of Hebrew and Ancient Greek Research interest in the processes of Inculturation in the liturgy Interest and experience in the fields of liturgy and ecumenism What we offer: The contract term for this position is 4 years. The employment contract, initially limited to 1.5 years, will be automatically extended to 4 years unless the employer issues a notice of non-renewal within the first 12 months. Work-life balance: 30 hours that can be distributed throughout the week. Inspiring working atmosphere: You are a part of an international academic team in a healthy and fair working environment. Good public transport connections: Your workplace is easily accessible by public transport. Internal further training & Coaching: Opportunity to deepen your skills on an ongoing basis. There are over 600 courses to choose from – free of charge. Fair salary: The basic salary of EUR 3.776,10 (on a full-time basis) increases if we can credit professional experience. Get off to a great start in your new job: the Welcome Compass helps you settle into your new role at the University of Vienna and life in Vienna. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! It is that easy to apply: Letter of motivation Academic curriculum vitae Brief dissertation proposal Master’s degree or diploma certificate Additional educational and degree certificates (if available) Via our job portal / “Apply Now” button If you have any content questions, please contact: Hans-Jürgen Feulner hans-juergen.feulner@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of  Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection Application deadline: 10/11/2026 Prae Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Requ