    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-Assistant-postdoctoral/1438413133/": {
      "title": "University Assistant postdoctoral",
      "description": "University Assistant postdoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University Assistant postdoctoral At the University of Vienna, almost 11,000 people work together on the big questions of the future. Approximately 7,700 of them are academic staff members. These are individuals who, with their curiosity and their continuous pursuit of excellence, engage in international cutting-edge research and teaching. With us, you will also find space to unfold your potential. We are looking for a/an ... University Assistant postdoctoral 30 Faculty of Catholic Theology Job vacancy starting: 11/02/2026 | Working hours:  40.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 lit. b (postdoc) Limited contract until: 10/31/2032 Job ID: 6225 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where over 7,700 brilliant minds have found a unique balance of freedom and support. Join us if you’re passionate about groundbreaking international research and academic excellence. Ready to be part of our team? Let’s shape the future together! Your personal sphere of play: The unit ‘Theology and History of the Eastern Churches’ has an international network and is a research-intensive department. We expect academic excellence and offer an inspiring and stimulating working environment, flexible working hours and excellent opportunities for professional development. As a postdoctoral university assistant, you will work in the research team together with Prof. Thomas Németh in this Department. Your responsibilities will include independent research in the field of theology and history of Eastern Churches, as well as assistance and support in teaching. We expect you to complete a further qualification thesis, combined with the acquisition of a teaching qualification (habilitation). In addition, you will support the Research focus of the Department. The position will be available to be taken up on 11/02/2026 and is limited until 10/31/2032. Your future tasks: You will be actively involved in research, teaching and administration, which means: You will develop an independent research profile You will be involved in the uni’s research projects You will prepare and complete a habilitation thesis You will publish internationally and give lectures You will independently hold courses in accordance with the provisions of the collective agreement You will be involved in student supervision and departmental administration This is part of your personality: Completion of basic studies and a doctorate in (Catholic) theology We also require the following as essential criteria: a very good command of English or German and a good command of the other language (which must be demonstrated within one year), as well as of a Slavic language or Modern Greek. Excellent knowledge of theology and history of the Orthodox Churches from the modern era to the present day; a specialisation is expected in the field of Eastern European or Caucasian church history of the 19th and 20th centuries. University teaching skills, preferably evidenced by relevant certificates, and experience in independently delivering university-level teaching, including digital formats Proficiency in Ancient Greek Experience in applying for and securing external funding Experience in the planning, organization and budgeting of academic conferences Publications in the field of Eastern church history Experience in university self-governance Further desirable qualities are: Experience in student support Experience with innovative forms of digital communication What we offer: You will be part of a stimulating and challenging, internationally networked research team A workplace in the heart of Vienna, with excellent public transport links Opportunities for further training and developing your skills A monthly salary of € 5.014,30 (paid 14 times a year) – in addition, relevant professional experience may influence your pay grade and therefore your remuneration. It is that easy to apply: Letter of motivation, including research interests Brief outline of the habilitation project Academic CV, including a list of publications, a list of courses taught, and lectures given Degree certificates; further documentation of proven skills If you have any questions, please contact: Thomas Mark Németh thomas.nemeth@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. University of Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection ​Application deadline: 10/02/2026 Post Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: postdoctoral Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session c