    "https://jobs.univie.ac.at/job/University-assistant-predoctoral/1438382033/": {
      "title": "University assistant predoctoral",
      "description": "University assistant predoctoral Job Details | Universität Wien We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Please note that you can see the videos on this website only if you accept all cookies! Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Careers UniVie All Vacancies Career UniVie Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling HR (E) IT (E) Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) All Vacancies Language (DE/EN) Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) Create Profile / Login & Logout Employee Login Search by Keyword Advanced Filter Options Loading... Job Category All Full / Part Time All General / Scientific Staff All Facility All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University assistant predoctoral At the University of Vienna almost 11,000 personalities work together towards answering the big questions of the future. Around 7,700  of them do research and teaching, around 3,000 work in administration and organisation. We are looking for a/an University assistant predoctoral 30 Faculty of Catholic Theology Job vacancy starting:  | Working hours: 30.00  | Classification CBA: §48 VwGr. B1 Grundstufe (praedoc) Limited contract until: Job ID: 6188 Explore and teach at the University of Vienna, where more than 7,700 academics thrive on curiosity in continuous exploration and help us better understand our world. Does this sound like you? Then join our accomplished team! Your personal sphere of influence and academic environment: The Department of Intercultural Philosophy of Religion at the Faculty of Catholic Theology at the University of Vienna is seeking to fill a pre-doctoral position 30 hours / limited to 4 years (start date preferably mid October to early November). In addition to the philosophy of religion, the department’s core research areas include philosophical anthropology and the history of philosophy. The department actively participates in research focused on intercultural, comparative, and global philosophy. Teaching includes introductions to the fundamental disciplines of philosophy, with a special focus on the contributions of religious traditions of thought. Your future tasks: You will actively participate in research, teaching, and administration, which means: Participating in research projects and scientific studies Contributing to publications, scientific articles, and presentations, such as conducting literature reviews, proofreading, formatting, and compiling bibliographies You are expected to sign a dissertation agreement within 12–18 months Participating in and independently conducting courses, where possible, in accordance with the provisions of the collective bargaining agreement Student advising Assisting with the organization of meetings, conferences, and symposia Participating in departmental, teaching, and research administration, such as helping to maintain the department’s website, providing support for the Moodle e-learning platform, and assisting with exam preparation and administration This is part of your personality / profile: Diploma's / Master’s degree in (Catholic) Theology or Philosophy Strong written and oral communication skills Excellent command of German Good written and spoken English Basic computer skills Ability to work well in a team What we offer: An inspiring work environment: You’ll be part of a small, dedicated research team with excellent research infrastructure. In-house training and coaching: We offer you ongoing opportunities to deepen your skills. Flexible working hours and limited remote work are possible by arrangement. Good public transportation access: Your new workplace is centrally located in Vienna and easily accessible by public transport. Fixed-term contract and fair salary: The employment duration is 4 years . Initially limited to 1.5 years, the employment relationship is automatically extended to 4 years if the employer does not terminate it within the first 12 months by submitting a non-extension declaration. The base salary of EUR 3,776.10 gross [\"brutto\"] (based on full-time; 14 payments per year) in accordance with the collective bargaining agreement will increase if we can take your professional experience into account. Equal opportunities for all: We welcome every additional/new personality to the team! To apply, please submit the following documents: A cover letter / letter of motivation, describing your personal interest in the position and the department’s research focus Academic résumé Degree certificates / Notices of completion of a master’s or diploma program Thesis (master’s or diploma thesis) as a PDF Brief proposal for a dissertation project / summary of your research interests List of publications, proof of teaching experience (if applicable) Via our job portal / “Apply Now” button If you have any content questions, please contact: the department info.ikrph@univie.ac.at , Organisational Assistant Mag. Agnes Leyrer agnes.leyrer@univie.ac.at or University Professor DDr. Isabella Guanzini isabella.guanzini@univie.ac.at We look forward to new personalities in our team! The University of Vienna has an anti-discriminatory employment policy and attaches great importance to equal opportunities , the advancement of women and diversity . We place particular emphasis on enhancing women’s representation among the academic and general university staff, particularly in leadership roles, and therefore expressly encourage qualified women to apply. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female candidates. We look forward to receiving your detailed application, including a motivational letter, under reference number 5965, preferably  via the job portal / \"Apply Now\" button, deadline mentioned below. University of  Vienna. Space for personalities. Since 1365. Data protection Application deadline: 10/11/2026 Prae Doc Apply now » Find similar jobs: predoctoral, Praedoc, Alle Jobangebote, All Vacancies Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral (Senior) Lecturer & Scientists (E) Tenure Track Professorships Full Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Howeve